|~ `::holds`, the kind of an invariant, and the laws declared under it.

   The decisions it exists for: [D189]. ~|

:holds
  |~~ An invariant is a query the values of a label keep, written as a
      quote under this tag and declared under the name it guards, the
      name of the refusal of a value that breaks it: after the
      declaration `:Small/TooLargeError ::holds~(lt 10)`, a value put
      under `::Small` is checked, and `::Small(12)` is refused under
      `::Small/TooLargeError`.

      An invariant guards a label, the args of a word, a part of them or
      a word's answer, by where it is declared, and runs when the value
      is built, read or answered; `is` of a kind and `every ~(is …)` are
      the invariants of kinds.
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|

:holds/refusesUnderItsName
  |~~ A value that breaks an invariant is refused under its name. ~~|
  ::law~(:Small |~~ Below ten. ~~| | :Small/TooLargeError ::holds~(lt 10) | [(::Small(3) | type) (::Small(12) !| type)] | eq [::Small ::Small/TooLargeError])
